{
  "dom_id": "step-q327277",
  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, we note that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})}=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})}=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$",
